    <statement><p>If <m>f(x) = x^3 + 6 x^2 - 36 x + 24</m>, find analytically all values of <m>x</m>
for which <m>f'(x) = 0</m>.  (Enter your answer as a comma separated
list of numbers, e.g., -1,0,2)</p>
<p><m>x =</m> <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2, -6</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>f(x) = x^3 + 6 x^2 - 36 x + 24</m>, we have 
<me>f'(x) = 3 x^2 + 12 x - 36 = 3 ( x^2 + 4 x - 12 ) = 
   3 (x - 2)(x + 6).</me>  
This is zero if <m>x = 2</m> or <m>x = -6</m>.



</solution>
